        {
          "path": "_m/t/c/1/x/nine-arch-bridge-wp/a-train-crosses-the-nine-arche.jpg",
          "filename": "A Train Crosses The Nine Arches Bridge (243270425).jpeg",
          "caption": "500px provided description: A blue train crosses the Nine Arches Bridge also called The Bridge in the sky, which is one of the most iconic bridges in Sri Lanka and is one of the best examples of British railway constructions when Ceylon was yet a colony of the British Empire. It is located in Demodara, between Ella and Demodara railway stations. At about 3100 feet above the sea level, this 99.6ft high bridge is built entirely of solid rocks, bricks and cement without using a single piece of steel. The bridge was commissioned in 1921.\n\nThe bridge's architectural ingenuity and the profuse greenery in the nearby hillsides likens it to the countryside through which the fictional Hogwarts express passes through in the Harry Potter world. [#trees ,#blue ,#outdoor ,#architecture ,#bridge ,#rocks ,#railway ,#500px ,#tunnel ,#hillside ,#estate ,#tea gardens ,#tea country ,#Canon ,#Train ,#Sri Lanka ,#Central Province ,#Asia ,#Rail ,#Tea ,#National Geographic ,#Ella ,#Ceylon ,#Lonely Planet ,#Angshuman ,#Demodara ,#Nine Arches Bridge ,#Nategeo_Traveller ,#central Sri Lanka]",
          "alt": "500px provided description: A blue train crosses the Nine Arches Bridge also called The Bridge in the sky, which is one of the most iconic bridges in Sri Lanka and is one of the best examples of British railway constructions when Ceylon was yet a colony of the British Empire. It is located in Demodara, between Ella and Demodara railway stations. At about 3100 feet above the sea level, this 99.6ft high bridge is built entirely of solid rocks, bricks and cement without using a single piece of steel. The bridge was commissioned in 1921.\n\nThe bridge's architectural ingenuity and the profuse greenery in the nearby hillsides likens it to the countryside through which the fictional Hogwarts express passes through in the Harry Potter world. [#trees ,#blue ,#outdoor ,#architecture ,#bridge ,#rocks ,#railway ,#500px ,#tunnel ,#hillside ,#estate ,#tea gardens ,#tea country ,#Canon ,#Train ,#Sri Lanka ,#Central Province ,#Asia ,#Rail ,#Tea ,#National Geographic ,#Ella ,#Ceylon ,#Lonely Planet ,#Angshuman ,#Demodara ,#Nine Arches Bridge ,#Nategeo_Traveller ,#central Sri Lanka]",
